<title>ITALY: Stet Jan-Apr sales above 13 trln lire - MD.</title>
<headline>Stet Jan-Apr sales above 13 trln lire - MD.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian state telecoms holding Stet is expected to have satisfactory results this year and sales on the first four months of 1997 were above 13 trillion lire, the company's managing director said.</p>
<p>Stet MD Tomaso Tommasi Di Vignano told a shareholders' meeting here 1997 results were expected to be &quot;definitely satisfactory&quot;.</p>
<p>He said financial debt stood at 10 trillion lire and investments at three trillion.  </p>
<p>Stet's sales were 40.5 trillion lire in 1996 and its net financial debt at the end of 1996 was 12.04 trillion.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +39 266129507</p>
</text>
